---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
import Readout from "~/components/Readout.astro";
import CtaBand from "~/components/CtaBand.astro";
import experiment from "~/data/experiment.json";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import { site } from "~/data/site";

const entries = (await getCollection("changelog")).sort(
  (a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf(),
);
const fmt = new Intl.NumberFormat("en-GB");
const opps = experiment.topOpportunities;
---
<Base
  title="Proof & method — the experiment running on this domain"
  description="The measurement method behind Autopilot: the published baseline, the holdout design, the measurement window, and what gets reported including the losses."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Proof", href: "/proof/" }]}
>
  <section class="section head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label">Proof &amp; method</p>
      <h1>The experiment is this website.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Selling an autonomous optimiser with a hand-built marketing site would be a
        contradiction. So mywebmaster.co.uk is the test subject: same system, same constraints,
        same published record — and the starting numbers were posted before any work began.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <Readout />
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow prose">
      <h2>What the baseline says</h2>
      <p>
        Over the 90 days to {experiment.baseline.window.endDate}, this domain was shown in
        Google results {fmt.format(experiment.baseline.impressions)} times and received
        {experiment.baseline.clicks} clicks — a click-through rate of
        {experiment.baseline.ctr}% at an average position of {experiment.baseline.position}.
      </p>
      <p>
        An average position near forty means the site is indexed and considered relevant, but
        sits three or four pages beyond where anyone looks. The impressions are real demand
        arriving and finding nothing. That is a more useful starting point than no traffic at
        all, because the demand does not have to be created — only served.
      </p>

      <h2>The demand that is already arriving</h2>
      <p>
        These are the queries where this domain earns impressions but almost no clicks. Note
        what they have in common: they describe the problem Autopilot exists to solve.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Query</th>
            <th scope="col">Impressions</th>
            <th scope="col">Clicks</th>
            <th scope="col">CTR</th>
            <th scope="col">Avg. position</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {opps.map((o) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{o.query}</th>
              <td class="num">{fmt.format(o.impressions)}</td>
              <td class="num">{o.clicks}</td>
              <td class="num">{o.ctr}%</td>
              <td class="num">{o.position}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="mono muted src">
      Source: Google Search Console, domain property, {experiment.baseline.window.startDate} to
      {experiment.baseline.window.endDate}, final data state.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section method invert">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label">Method</p>
      <h2>How a result gets called a result</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--2 steps">
        <div class="card">
          <p class="mono n">01</p>
          <h3>Publish the baseline first</h3>
          <p class="muted">Recorded before any change ships, from final-state data so it cannot drift. It removes the option of picking a flattering start date after the fact.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <p class="mono n">02</p>
          <h3>Split into treatment and control</h3>
          <p class="muted">Comparable pages are randomly assigned. The control group is deliberately left unoptimised, which costs real value and buys a trustworthy number.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <p class="mono n">03</p>
          <h3>Fix the window before looking</h3>
          <p class="muted">28 days, chosen in advance, with the page frozen throughout. Anything shorter measures noise; anything chosen afterwards measures wishful thinking.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <p class="mono n">04</p>
          <h3>Report the difference, losses included</h3>
          <p class="muted">Treatment movement minus control movement. Changes that lose are reverted and published with the same prominence as the ones that win.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow prose">
      <h2>What we cannot claim yet</h2>
      <p>
        This experiment started on {experiment.baseline.capturedAt}. Search results move slowly:
        a change takes weeks to settle, and a control comparison needs a full measurement window
        before it says anything. Any provider showing you dramatic results within days of
        starting is showing you variance.
      </p>
      <p>
        So there is currently one honest claim on this page: here is the starting line, here is
        the method, and here is the log. The next readout publishes when the first window closes
        — whether or not the numbers flatter us.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/changelog/">Read the {entries.length} changes made so far →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    heading="Want the same experiment run on your site?"
    body="It starts the same way: a published baseline, a control group, and a fixed window. No graph without a control group."
  />
</Base>

<style>
  .head h1 { margin-block: 1rem 1.2rem; max-width: 16ch; }
  table { min-width: 640px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-strong); }
  .num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.82rem; }
  th[scope="row"] { font-weight: 500; }
  .src { margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.7rem; }
  .method h2 { margin-block: 0.8rem 2rem; }
  .steps h3 { font-size: var(--step-1); margin-block: 0.4rem 0.6rem; }
  .steps p { font-size: var(--step--1); }
  .steps .n { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.1em; }
  .prose a { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
</style>
